1
00:00:03,208 --> 00:00:09,072
Cyber Monday returns arrive all through December and January, and without grading every box

2
00:00:09,072 --> 00:00:13,518
goes straight back to shelf or costs more to handle than it is worth.

3
00:00:13,968 --> 00:00:20,856
Return Arcs draws the whole reverse-logistics flow as boomerang arcs flying in from

4
00:00:20,856 --> 00:00:26,748
four regions to a central dock and fanning out to six disposition bays.

5
00:00:27,875 --> 00:00:31,590
Arc thickness shows unit volume, dash speed tracks age, and

6
00:00:31,590 --> 00:00:34,675
arc height out of the dock is net recovery value.

7
00:00:35,125 --> 00:00:38,662
Switch to the recovery lens and scrap arcs sag visibly

8
00:00:38,662 --> 00:00:43,115
below the zero-dollar baseline so value loss stands out immediately.

9
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:50,288
Today ranks what needs attention right now: nine returns past the forty-eight-hour grading target,

10
00:00:50,288 --> 00:00:55,878
four write-offs and high refunds waiting for the lead, and five returnless candidates.

11
00:00:56,328 --> 00:00:59,874
Selecting the overdue cohort dims everything else and highlights

12
00:00:59,874 --> 00:01:02,478
the withering dashes still sitting at the dock.

13
00:01:03,288 --> 00:01:08,421
Switching View As to Grader brings ungraded dock arrivals forward; Returns Lead

14
00:01:08,421 --> 00:01:13,618
dims them to spotlight pending write-offs and refunds over five hundred dollars.

15
00:01:14,419 --> 00:01:18,722
At the Dock, entering a twelve-dollar mug with seven dollars of

16
00:01:18,722 --> 00:01:23,639
handling triggers Rule Three immediately and offers a returnless refund.

17
00:01:24,089 --> 00:01:29,522
The same form checks the holiday return window: November twenty-eighth orders stay in window

18
00:01:29,522 --> 00:01:35,369
through January thirty-first, while December twenty-eighth orders past thirty days are marked late.

19
00:01:36,172 --> 00:01:39,961
On the Grading bench, a customer with five returns out of ten

20
00:01:39,961 --> 00:01:45,862
orders surfaces a fifty-percent repeat-returner banner for awareness without ever auto-denying.

21
00:01:46,671 --> 00:01:51,442
At the Fork, the recovery ladder computes every bay side by side. For

22
00:01:51,442 --> 00:01:56,421
a Grade C return, Restock is locked out with the exact rule explanation.

23
00:01:57,275 --> 00:02:02,385
Finally, in the Write-off book, a six-hundred-twenty-dollar projector refund stays

24
00:02:02,385 --> 00:02:05,875
pending until the Returns lead approves and releases it.

25
00:02:07,826 --> 00:02:11,129
Return Arcs: every return graded on time, routed to

26
00:02:11,129 --> 00:02:14,756
its highest recovery value, and governed by clear rules.
